specan_ui — graphical real-time spectrum analyzer for the Ubertooth.

Requirements:
  * Python 3.8 or newer. Every feature works on 3.8; on an older interpreter
    the build skips the Python tools.
  * Python packages: numpy, qtpy, and one Qt binding, PySide6 or PyQt5. The
    Python version only limits which binding release you can install:
      - pip: `pip install numpy qtpy pyside6` picks a PySide6 that supports
        your Python (6.6 on Python 3.8).
      - apt (Debian/Ubuntu): `python3-numpy python3-qtpy python3-pyqt5`.
        Ubuntu has no python3-pyside6 package before 24.10.
  * The built Ubertooth host tools (provides ubertooth-specan)

Install (installs the launcher AND the specan Python package):
  $ cd host/build && cmake .. && make && sudo make install

Run:
  $ ubertooth-specan-ui          # or: sudo ubertooth-specan-ui  (device access)

Getting "ModuleNotFoundError: No module named 'specan'"? Install with
install.sh or `make install`, and check `which -a ubertooth-specan-ui` for a
stale launcher earlier on PATH. See the full guide:

  docs/source/specan_ui.rst
  (https://ubertooth.readthedocs.io/en/latest/specan_ui.html)
